<title>ISRAEL: Clal Israel Q3 EPS 0.05 shekel vs 2.33.</title>
<headline>Clal Israel Q3 EPS 0.05 shekel vs 2.33.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Clal Israel Ltd.</p>
<p>			   (in thousands of shekels except EPS)</p>
<p>			    Q3 96	Q3 95     9-MTH 96  9-MTH 95</p>
<p>Revenue		   1,314,546  1,360,958 3,980,490 3,882,881</p>
<p>Pre-tax Profit	     20,553     32,314    82,379    35,606</p>
<p>Net Profit		    1,590     72,852   110,462   150,640</p>
<p>Earnings per Share	   0.05	 2.33	3.56	4.87</p>
<p>Clal, one of Israel's leading holding companies, said profitability was hit by steeper losses at Scitex Corporation Ltd and Sunfrost Ltd as well as weaker earnings at Kitan Consolidated Ltd and Cargal Ltd.</p>
<p>But it said in a statement that its insurance and building materials businesses had reported improved results.</p>
<p>Clal said an agreement this week in the high-tech sector under which its subsidiary Clal Electronics Industries will sell its 30 percent stake in Opal Inc to Applied Materials Inc for $50 million would be reflected in future financial statements.</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
